  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_020: scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + concat → acc 0.507), evidence is extremely sparse. The most informative next step is a single-variable A/B test on the fusion strategy, since fusion is the final integration step and likely has outsized impact on how well the two modalities are combined. config_032 is identical to config_020 except fusion changes from concat to weighted. This directly clarifies whether weighted fusion (which learns a scalar reweighting of the two modalities) outperforms simple concatenation under the same backbone. If weighted wins, we gain a strong signal to explore weighted-fusion variants across encoders; if concat wins or ties, we can rule out fusion as a bottleneck and pivot to testing aggregation (avgpool vs transformer) or RNA encoder choice. This minimal-change comparison maximally reduces uncertainty about a critical design axis with one experiment, preserving budget for subsequent exploitation."
}

